  "articleBody": "Thinking about making your kitchen more accessible? It's a fantastic way to make your home more comfortable and functional for everyone. When you're planning these updates, you'll want to focus on a few key areas to ensure the layout really works. First, consider reach ranges and sight lines – you want frequently used items to be easy to grab without stretching or bending too much. Then, think about traffic paths; clear floor space is crucial, especially if you're using a wheelchair. Don't forget storage zones, either; pull-out shelves or lowered cabinets can make a huge difference. Lighting is another often-overlooked aspect that can greatly improve usability. Finally, review appliance placement to make sure everything is easily reachable and usable. HH Remodeling LLC specializes in disability and accessibility modifications, and we're here to help you coordinate all these elements so they work together seamlessly for your unique needs. We serve the greater Denver area, including Aurora, Denver, Centennial, and many other surrounding communities. Getting professional advice can really help you nail down a design that’s perfect for you.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}